,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Submitting author:** <!--author-handle-->@pmocz<!--end-author-handle--> (<a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-6631-2566\">Philip Mocz</a>)\n**Repository:** <!--target-repository-->https://github.com/JaxionProject/jaxion<!--end-target-repository-->\n**Branch with paper.md** (empty if default branch): <!--branch--><!--end-branch-->\n**Version:** <!--version-->0.0.3<!--end-version-->\n**Editor:** <!--editor-->@arfon<!--end-editor-->\n**Reviewers:** <!--reviewers-list-->@shubhagrawal30, @chaitanyaafle<!--end-reviewers-list-->\n**Archive:** <!--archive-->10.5281/zenodo.21221061<!--end-archive-->\n\n## Status\n\n[![status](https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084/status.svg)](https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084)\n\nStatus badge code:\n\n```\nHTML: <a href=\"https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084\"><img src=\"https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084/status.svg\"></a>\nMarkdown: [![status](https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084/status.svg)](https://joss.theoj.org/papers/a6a54a472e31926b25606cf281f5d084)\n```\n**Reviewers and authors**:\n\nPlease avoid lengthy details of difficulties in the review thread. Instead, please create a new issue in the <a href=\"https://github.com/JaxionProject/jaxion\" target=\"_blank\">target repository</a> and link to those issues (especially acceptance-blockers) by leaving comments in the review thread below. (For completists: if the target issue tracker is also on GitHub, linking the review thread in the issue or vice versa will create corresponding breadcrumb trails in the link target.)\n\n## Reviewer instructions & questions\n\n@jordydavelaar & @shubhagrawal30, your review will be checklist based. Each of you will have a separate checklist that you should update when carrying out your review.\nFirst of all you need to run this command in a separate comment to create the checklist:\n\n```\n@editorialbot generate my checklist\n```\n\nThe reviewer guidelines are available here: https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/reviewer_guidelines.html. Any questions/concerns please let @arfon know.\n\n✨ **Please start on your review when you are able, and be sure to complete your review in the next six weeks, at the very latest** ✨ \n\n\n## Checklists\n\n<!--checklist-comments-->\n<!--checklist-for-shubhagrawal30-->\n📝 [Checklist for @shubhagrawal30](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9542#issuecomment-3621517164)\n<!--end-checklist-for-shubhagrawal30-->\n<!--checklist-for-chaitanyaafle-->\n📝 [Checklist for @chaitanyaafle](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9542#issuecomment-4413632611)\n<!--end-checklist-for-chaitanyaafle-->\n<!--end-checklist-comments-->\n","closed_by":{"login":"arfon","id":4483,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon","html_url":"https://github.com/arfon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/us